{#
  apt takes the first stanza that matches a version:
  - Ubuntu's nginx packages are never installed;
  - nginx.org's versions of the series win (with or without an epoch);
  - any other version (another series) is never installed.
  Without nginx.org's package lists there is no candidate, and the install
  fails instead of falling back to Ubuntu's nginx.
#}
Explanation: managed by noixdev.infra (nginx role). Changes here are overwritten.
Package: {{ nginx_apt_packages }}
Pin: release o=Ubuntu
Pin-Priority: -1

Package: {{ nginx_apt_packages }}
Pin: version /^([0-9]+:)?{{ nginx_version | regex_escape }}\./
Pin-Priority: 990

Package: {{ nginx_apt_packages }}
Pin: version *
Pin-Priority: -1
